{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design", "label": "describe-it Design Specification (2026-08-19)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_single_user_message_prompt", "label": "Single user message, no system prompt", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Several small vision models ignore or mishandle system prompts, so the built-in wording (max_words, language, optional context sentence) goes in one user message ending 'Reply with the alt text only'; the wording forbids opening with 'image of'/'picture of'/'photo of'."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_non_goals_v01", "label": "Non-goals for v0.1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Async API, streaming, batching, non-Ollama backends, result caching, automatic model pulling, guaranteed output length, vision-capability detection (Ollama returns a clear error surfaced as OllamaResponseError)."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_pr_stack_work_units", "label": "Three-PR stack of work units", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "1 scaffold + pure layers (exceptions, image, prompt, CI); 2 client + describer + fake-server fixture; 3 CLI, integration tests, README, ARCHITECTURE, ADRs, live run recorded in the PR body."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_open_questions_sign_off", "label": "Open questions Q1-Q4 and resolutions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Q1 default model -> qwen3.5:4b; Q2 GitHub -> private Xof/describe-it with PR stack and Actions CI; Q3 Python floor -> >=3.12 with 3.12/3.13/3.14 matrix; Q4 refusal strictness -> guarded heuristic."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_errata_units_1_3", "label": "Errata found during units 1-3 (2026-08-20)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Corrections discovered while implementing: fixed-point cleaning, guard rule on cleaned text, wide-mode rescale, EXIF, colour keys, non-finite samples, client= seam, validation at construction, proxy/redirect opener, host normalisation, CLI argparse types, one-line-per-file escaping, broken-pipe handling, live-test env-check order, py.typed metadata."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_cli_one_line_per_file_contract", "label": "CLI one-line-per-file output contract", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every control character (C0, DEL, C1) is escaped in the description, the path and failure text, and backslashes in paths doubled, because none of the three is trusted: a tab forges a column, CR/LF split a record, ESC carries a terminal escape. clean_response is left alone since this is presentation. Failures are 'describe-it: <path>: <reason>' with whitespace collapsed. DecompressionBombWarning suppressed; each description flushed as produced."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_broken_pipe_handling", "label": "Missing and closed output stream handling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With sys.stdout None there is nowhere to deliver a description, so exit 1 without work; with no stderr diagnostics are dropped. A closed pipe exits 1 quietly: both streams flushed explicitly before main returns (the interpreter's exit flush cannot handle BrokenPipeError), and only the broken stream's descriptor is pointed at /dev/null. stdout is the product, stderr is commentary."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_argparse_type_validation", "label": "Option validation via argparse type functions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every value the library can reject is validated by an argparse type function so a bad one is a usage message and exit 2 rather than a traceback; --model and --host default to None so the env vars mean the same on the command line, and main turns the ValueError they can still raise into the same usage error."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_client_injection_seam", "label": "client= keyword as test seam", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Describer/describe() accept a ready-made OllamaClient so the suite can drive the real urllib path against an in-process server; supported public surface but not the simple-API story. Skips host/timeout validation."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design", "target": "github_workflows_ci", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design", "target": "readme", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design", "target": "architecture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_single_user_message_prompt", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_non_goals_v01", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_19_describe_it_design_pr_stack_work_units", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-describe-it-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "do